# JDBC thin 11.2 (ojdbc6) writing aa bb cc at offset 3 into a BLOB fetched FOR
# UPDATE on 10.2.0.5 (#2803): the LOBOPS WRITE, with its amount (3 bytes), and
# the LOB_DATA message behind it.
# Captured 2026-11-27 through tools/capture_proxy.py. The TTC payload,
# without the packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column
# and the |ascii| gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
00000000  03 60 08 01 01 56 00 00  00 00 00 00 00 01 40 00  |.`...V........@.|
00000010  00 01 03 00 01 00 00 00  00 00 00 00 54 00 01 01  |............T...|
00000020  0c 00 00 00 01 00 00 00  01 00 00 00 2e 69 d8 00  |.............i..|
00000030  05 76 a7 00 05 76 a4 00  03 00 03 00 00 00 01 01  |.v...v..........|
00000040  02 03 04 05 06 07 08 00  65 00 66 00 00 00 00 00  |........e.f.....|
00000050  cf fc bb 00 00 00 03 00  1f 00 00 15 be 00 80 07  |................|
00000060  69 04 78 3f 00 00 00 00  05 76 a4 00 40 62 6a 00  |i.x?.....v..@bj.|
00000070  00 01 03 0e 03 aa bb cc                           |........|
